From 0c98323ebe27d8222a1d66fdebf1463366c5bf2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Terrydaktal <9lewis9@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 05:31:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Publish serial GDN arithmetic contract and speculative
 reference adapters

Provide the pinned stock-FLA oracle and ordered Triton scan used to diagnose and repair serial/speculative state divergence. Preserve BF16 beta rounding, stock normalization and reduction operations, persistent FP32 state and output conversion rather than silently selecting a different numerical target.

Include convolution, prefill, recurrent and indexed adapters, per-row state selection and native differential replay. Explicitly distinguish processed verification rows from the newly emitted pending token and retain independent state for accepted prefixes. Add source provenance, the immutable reference contract and CPU ownership/admission regressions with negative controls.

Validation: 78 CPU checks passed; one retained compiler-artifact check was explicitly skipped. Copied runtime sources match the qualified downstream identities. The complete compiled Radiance integration has separate 10K evidence; this bundle supplies a test oracle for an upstream HIP port and does not claim that production libr4d has already been converted or qualified.
Link the experiment README directly to the public report and aggregate
evidence so the prepared upstream submission is reviewable without private
repository access. This documentation update changes no measured kernel.

Signed-off-by: Terrydaktal <9lewis9@gmail.com>
