+# Serial GDN contract and speculative reference
+
+This bundle supplies the tested stock-FLA arithmetic reference and adapters used
+to localize and repair M1/M8 disagreement. It is an experimental reference for a
+libr4d port, **not a completed HIP replacement in libr4d's public dispatcher**.
+The complete tested Radiance integration is in
+[Radiance #11](https://github.com/magiccodingman/vllm-radiance/pull/11).
+
+```text
+experimental/serial_gdn_contract/
+├── reference-contract.json       # immutable finite-precision specification and artifact hashes
+├── stock_gdn_sequence.py         # pinned native M1 oracle and private after-row state
+├── stock_gdn_scan_kernel.py      # ordered Triton transition with the same arithmetic
+├── stock_gdn_scan.py             # scan admission and retained-state selection
+├── stock_gdn_*adapter.py         # convolution, prefill, recurrence and indexed calls
+├── probe_stock_gdn_sequence.py   # native differential replay and negative controls
+├── tests/                       # CPU state/ownership/admission regressions
+└── SOURCE_PROVENANCE.json        # downstream source identities
+```
+
+Unlike the R4D-M1 prefill reference, this contract rounds sigmoid beta through
+BF16, uses the stock reduction/normalization operations and uses the stock output
+rounding. A higher-precision beta is a different target, even if it appears more
+accurate in isolation. The preserved contract's historical status fields are
+not rewritten: its hash identifies the reference definition, while later
+qualification receipts record what was subsequently tested.
+
+Row zero processes the previously emitted pending token. For k accepted proposals
+(0 through 7), commit state after row k; the newly emitted correction or bonus
+token is pending, not prematurely consumed. Rejected rows cannot modify the
+retained prefix. The scan retains each state tile in registers across its ordered
+token loop, preserving transitions without eight separate whole-model launches.
+
+The support package from [Radiance #10](https://github.com/magiccodingman/vllm-radiance/pull/10)
+is required. With its checkout path in `RADIANCE`, run the CPU suite from this
+repository root:
+
+```sh
+uv run --project "$RADIANCE/benchmarks/conformance" --extra cpu-tests \
+  pytest experimental/serial_gdn_contract/tests -q
+```
+
+These tests exercise the actual coordination code with deliberate CPU stand-ins;
+they do not pretend the stand-ins perform GDN arithmetic. The optional native
+compiler-identity check needs preserved HSACO/metadata through
+`RADIANCE_GDN_REFERENCE_ARTIFACTS`; an absent artifact is an explicit skip.
+
+Native replay needs the pinned ROCm/vLLM environment, original source/compiler
+artifacts, authenticated synthetic capture and the shared exclusive GPU lease.
+The companion Radiance repair package supplies the remaining probe helpers.
+Consult `probe_stock_gdn_sequence.py --help` before admitting GPU execution.
+The native serial coordinator previously passed 38 exact state/output checks and
+detected both injected faults. The final compiled integration subsequently
+matched top-1/10/20 membership, ordering and full-logit digests at all 10,000
+positions, plus 23 prefills. That full result includes other stage repairs and
+must not be attributed to GDN alone.
+
+Remaining work for a production libr4d port: choose and preserve this declared
+contract in HIP, add the appropriate public dispatch/bindings, repeat native
+state/acceptance/graph checks, then perform complete model and speed qualification.
+The reference is provided so that work has a precise test oracle.
+
+[Report and compiled stage breakdown](https://github.com/Terrydaktal/d7-rdna4-report/blob/main/reports/d7-rdna4-2026-09-17/REPORT.md).
